 8/Industrial-Growth-Series-banner-1.jpg.jpeg?ver=1786471191
UID:r6EDrLGaL-T9FPHEt1k_r
SUMMARY:Industrial Growth Series: Why Great Industrial Companies Stop Growi
	ng
DTSTAMP:20260818T032840Z
DTSTART:20260824T120000Z
DESCRIPTION:Register here: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1996106693855?aff=o
	ddtdtcreator \nGreat industrial companies do not usually stop growing beca
	use they lack capability.\nThey stop growing because the market changes ar
	ound them.\nFor years\, many industrial companies have grown through stron
	g relationships\, repeat customers\, referrals\, reputation\, and word of 
	mouth.\nThat approach can work for a long time.\nUntil it does not.\nThe c
	ompany is still strong.\nThe team still delivers.\nCustomers still trust t
	he work.\nThe reputation is still solid.\nBut new opportunities become har
	der to create.\nThe same relationships are no longer producing the same vo
	lume of business. Referrals become less predictable. Buyers become harder 
	to reach. Competitors become more visible. The company starts depending to
	o heavily on the momentum it built in the past.\nThat is where many great 
	industrial companies get stuck.\nThey are not failing.\nThey have simply r
	eached a point where the way they grew before may not be enough to support
	 where they want to go next.\nThis session of the Industrial Growth Series
	 is designed to help owners\, executives\, and commercial leaders understa
	nd why strong industrial companies hit growth ceilings and what must begin
	 to change to create new momentum.\nWe will explore the role of market pos
	itioning\, visibility\, relationships\, business development\, diversifica
	tion\, and changing buyer behavior without turning the conversation into a
	nother tactical sales seminar.\nThis is not about chasing every opportunit
	y.\nIt is not about abandoning the relationships that helped build the com
	pany.\nIt is about recognizing when the market has changed and ensuring th
	e company’s approach to growth changes with it.\nWhat You’ll Learn\nWhy su
	ccessful industrial companies eventually hit growth ceilings\nWhy reputati
	on\, referrals\, and repeat customers may stop producing the same results\
	nHow changing markets and buyer behavior affect industrial growth\nWhere c
	ommercial momentum commonly begins to slow\nWhy strong capabilities do not
	 always create strong market visibility\nHow leaders can begin creating ne
	w paths to growth\nWhat established companies should evaluate before inves
	ting in more activity \nWho Should Attend\nIndustrial company owners and C
	EOs\nManufacturing leaders\nEnergy\, oil and gas\, and field service compa
	nies\nConstruction and infrastructure firms\nCommercial\, sales\, and busi
	ness development leaders\nCompanies with strong capabilities but inconsist
	ent new opportunity flow\nLeaders working to break through a growth platea
	u \nEvent Format\n11:45 AM – 12:00 PM | Networking at the stairs\n12:00 PM
	 – 12:40 PM | Presentation\n12:40 PM – 1:00 PM | Discussion and Q&A\n1:00 
	PM – 1:15 PM | Networking at the stairs \nAbout the Speaker\nJada Powell i
	s the Founder of Powell Consulting Group\, where she works with industrial
	\, energy\, oil and gas\, construction\, and service-based companies to bu
	ild stronger commercial infrastructure and more consistent business develo
	pment momentum.\nHer work focuses on helping mid-market companies move bey
	ond relationship-only growth into more intentional\, visible\, and scalabl
	e commercial strategies.\nThis session is part of the Industrial Growth Se
	ries\, a three-part in-person series at The Ion focused on how established
	 industrial companies can remain visible\, competitive\, and positioned fo
	r the next stage of growth.\n\nhttps://iondistrict.com/event/industrial-gr
	owth-series-why-great-industrial-companies-stop-growing/\n\nFrom Ion Distr
	ict
URL:https://iondistrict.com/event/industrial-growth-series-why-great-indust
	rial-companies-stop-growing/
